  "_comment": [
    "GAZETTEER — the authoritative entity list. This is the ONE place that decides",
    "what is a proper noun, because neither the source lexicon's casing nor an",
    "English dictionary can tell you:",
    "  - source casing is arbitrary  (source had 'arif' AND 'afzal' both lowercase,",
    "    yet 'Arif' ended up capitalised and 'afzal' did not)",
    "  - English dict says 'Delhi', 'Allah', 'Apple' are dictionary words (they are,",
    "    as proper nouns) while calling Urdu words like 'aasman' non-words",
    "Everything listed here is categorised as a proper noun and Title-Cased.",
    "Anything NOT listed falls through to 'words'. Extend this file as new names,",
    "places, doctors, labs or brands appear in the calls."
